## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical zero-trust for admin access, mirroring real enterprise risk of credential theft and lateral movement in hybrid environments.

## Key Concepts
- Zero-trust, device posture, MFA, PIM, Just-In-Time
- Jump hosts, session recording, RBAC, break-glass, SIEM/audit

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-policy: grant only if posture true and MFA passed
if (device.posture && user.mfa && time.inWindow) {
  grantAccess();
} else {
  denyAccess();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure effectiveness (MTTR, number of break-glass events)?
- How would this adapt to cloud-native IAM vs PAM solutions across AWS/Azure?

This question tests CISSP-aligned incident response and forensics skills in a serverless, multi-cloud context. It evaluates understanding of detection telemetry, containment procedures, evidence handling, chain of custody maintenance, and cross-provider playbooks.

Key Concepts

- Incident response lifecycles across AWS Lambda, Google Cloud Functions, and on-premises FaaS
- Evidence preservation and time synchronization across cloud providers
- Cross-cloud playbooks and tooling coordination

Code Example

```javascript
// Example: mock evidence hash calculation
const crypto = require('crypto');

function calculateEvidenceHash(filePath, content) {
  const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256');
  hash.update(content);
  const evidenceHash = hash.digest('hex');

  return {
    filePath,
    evidenceHash,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  };
}

module.exports = { calculateEvidenceHash };
```
